<h2>Match Validator</h2>
<p>Require two fields to have the same value before the form can be submitted — password confirmation, email confirmation, and similar "type it again" patterns.</p>

<div class="demo-box">
  <form onsubmit="event.preventDefault()">
    <div data-controller="match-validator">
      <label for="password">Password</label>
      <input
        id="password"
        type="password"
        name="user[password]"
        autocomplete="new-password"
        data-match-validator-target="field"
        data-action="input->match-validator#validate"
      />
      <br>

      <label for="password_confirmation">Confirm password</label>
      <input
        id="password_confirmation"
        type="password"
        name="user[password_confirmation]"
        autocomplete="new-password"
        data-match-validator-target="match"
        data-action="input->match-validator#validate"
      />

      <p data-match-validator-target="error" hidden>Passwords don't match.</p>
    </div>

    <button type="submit">Sign up</button>
  </form>
</div>

<h3>Case-insensitive match</h3>
<p>Set <code>data-match-validator-case-sensitive-value="false"</code> to ignore letter case — useful for email confirmation, where "Name@Example.com" and "name@example.com" should be treated as the same address.</p>

<div class="demo-box">
  <form onsubmit="event.preventDefault()">
    <div data-controller="match-validator" data-match-validator-case-sensitive-value="false">
      <label for="email">Email</label>
      <input
        id="email"
        type="email"
        name="user[email]"
        data-match-validator-target="field"
        data-action="input->match-validator#validate"
      />
      <br>

      <label for="email_confirmation">Confirm email</label>
      <input
        id="email_confirmation"
        type="email"
        name="user[email_confirmation]"
        data-match-validator-target="match"
        data-action="input->match-validator#validate"
      />

      <p data-match-validator-target="error" hidden>Emails don't match.</p>
    </div>

    <button type="submit">Sign up</button>
  </form>
</div>
